        <p>WRITE SILK PARTY DRESS.</p>
        <p>In our sketch is shewn a dainty little party dress of soft white silk. The full skirt is closely gathered over the hips, and trimmed at the hem with two full frills edged with a narrow frill of Valenciennes lace and a wider row of insertion to match. The bodice is gathered about the yoke, and is drawa up to the neck and finished</p>
        <p>with a tiny frill of lace. Over the bodice there is a deep, full berth° of the silk, edged with lace and insertion. Over this there are bretelles of pale turquoise blue ribbon. These are attached to a belt of the same ribbon, and are arranged in a bow at each side of the yoke and where they meet the belt.</p>
