      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-21_WidnesExaminer_art0122" n="art0122">
        <p>THE COMPTON HOUSE,</p>
        <p>LIVERPOOL.</p>
        <p>STOCKS OF NEW AND 'SUPERIOR WINTER GOODS,</p>
        <p>EXPRESSLY PURCHASED FOR THE 1907 CHRISTMAS MARKET, SURPASS, IN MAGNITUDE, VARIETY, AND MONEY VALUE, ANY THAT HAVE EVER BEEN ACCUMULATED WITHIN THESE WALLS.</p>
        <p>Quite in addition to the Immense Regular Stocks, a large number of Exceptional Purchases have been made upon terms so advantageous, that there is scarcely a Department of the Establishment that Is not in a position to offer NEW GOODS OF THE SEASON CONSIDERABLY BELOW PRICES CURRENT. AN INCOMPARABLE SELECTION OF NOVELTIES, NEW FASHIONS, AND USEFUL WINTER GOODS.</p>
        <p>THOUSANDS OF PRETTY ARTICLES in sterling Silver; Artistic Silver-plated Pieces for the Table; Richly-mounted Dressing Cases in morocco, &amp;c.; Travelling Bags, Hand Bags, Dress Baskets, Rugs; AN ENORMOUS SELECTION of Christmas Cards, Calendars, Children's Picture Books, Presentation Volumes, Table Decorations, Fancy Xmas Stationery, and Fancy Articles; CHARMING SPECIMENS of Art Needlework (various), Fans, &amp;c.; EXQUISITE NEW PRO- DUCTIONS in Real and Machine Laces; PRETTY MADE-UP THINGS in Silk, Chiffon, Net, and other Fabrics ; Novelties in Ladies' Belts, Neck- ties, Head and Shoulder Wraps, Umbrellas, Gloves; Fancy, Warm, and Useful Hose and Woven Under- wear; Ladies' Underlinen and Underclothing in Winter Materials; Aprons, Handkerchiefs, Ribbons, Flowers, Feather Stoles, Plumes, Hair Decorations, and Fancy Drapery without end; LADIES' EVEN- ING GOWNS, Blouses, Opera Wraps, and Dress Wear of all kinds for Ladies, Gentlemen, and all Young PeopIe;STYLISH MADE-UP GARMENTS, lin all the Latest Modes, for Home Wear, Walk- ing,Visiting,Travelling,Motoring.and all purposes,in Silks and all fashionable textures ; LOVELY FUR GARMENTS in rich Sables and all favourite skins; DAINTY CHRISTMAS MILLINERY for all ages and all purposes; Ready-made Clothing, Hosiery, Underwear, and OUTFITTING FOR GENTLE- MEN and Boys; Footwear in all the most renowned brands, English, American, and Con- tinental, Dainty and Useful Furniture, and British and Foleign Fancy Articles, in a thousand forms ; an Enormous Selection of Christmas Glass, China, Earthenware rable Cutlery in dozens or PRESEN- TATION CASES ; Iron, Brass, Cooper, Aluminium, Tin and Enamelled Steel Home Requirements; Curtains and other CHRISTMAS DECORATIONS; Table Linens, House Linens, Bedclothing, and all kinds of Drapery; Warm, Useful, and Inexpensive Drapery FOR CHARITIES; Toys, Dolls, Games, Tovelties, and Specialities in thousands for the</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-21_WidnesExaminer_art0123" n="art0123">
