        <p>W ARRINGTON UNION NV ORIKHOUSE. --- lIRSIDRNT MEDICAL OFFICER. THE GUARDIANS of the WARRINGTog UNION INVITE APPLICATIONS from MEDIC:AL GENTLEMEN for the appointment of RESIDENT MEDICAL OFFICER. The average number of Inmates is about 500. The number of beds in the Infirmary about 200. Applicants must be single or widowers duly registered under the Medical Acts and legally qualified to practice both Medicine and surgery in England and Wales. Production of licences, Diplomas, Certificates &amp;c., will be necessary when the Guardians apply for same. The appointment will he subject to the provisions of The Poor Law Officers' Superannuation Act, 1896 Salary £l5O per annum aud vaccination fees, with apartments, rations and other usual allowances. The duties will include Lectures &amp;c. to Nurses, Medical Attendance upon the Indoor Official Staff and general compliance with the Local Government Orders. Medicines, Surgical Appliances, Sco will be pro- vided by the Guardians. Applications ars to be mate on forms to be obtained from me upon my receipt of a request for same such to be remrned to me by Post filled up before Noon on January 7th. 1903. Canvassing the Guardians will be strictly prohibited. J. C. SUTTON, Clerk to the Guardians. Bewsey Chambe-s, Warrington.</p>
